# r1113 chunk 3, rerun of boot c3a1's batch faults (verdicts: perf/runs/r1113/verdicts/c3a1.md). Fresh boot, World
# group A superflat, full pack (ground top y -61, stand at -60). Level name: fixc3a1.
# Setup before boot (server stopped):
#   bash tools/scratch_query/prep_srv.sh OUT fixc3a1 A difficulty=normal
#   cp $INST/tools/scratch_query/c3_probe.js   OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_c3_probe.js    (/zc3)
#   cp $INST/tools/scratch_query/zp_probe.js   OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_zp_probe.js    (/zp)
#   cp $INST/tools/scratch_query/zact_probe.js OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_zact_probe.js  (/zact; needs the
#     2026-11-13 copy with `break ... keep`)
#   (zq is copied by prep_srv.sh). No config edit before boot; FCK-13 and IP-05 edit configs live and restore them.
# Fixes against c3_a1.qb:
#   - `zc3 aim` threw (BotPlayer has no setYRot in Rhino): aims are `execute as BOT at @s run tp @s ~ ~ ~ YAW PITCH`.
#   - Live config edits: `sed -i` replaces the file (new inode) and Forge's watcher never fired (no "changed, sending
#     notifies" in debug.log); edits now rewrite the same file (sed > tmp, cat tmp > file).
#   - MG-22 upper half is coffee_bush[half=upper] (coffee_bush_top is the stem top; the bush died at once on setblock).
#   - AZW-03 bark is a chance output: read with rdetail (rdetail+ results), not `makes`.
#   - BOT-03 pot filled by data merge (a right-click on a pot without growth opens its menu, nothing was inserted).
#   - FCK-09 one rdetail per feast can (the prefix query hit rdetail's 40-line cut).
#   - FCK-11 bot stands at the well; the can's WaterLevel read before and after.
#   - FCB-09 broken with a pickaxe (copper pot dropped no item bare-handed) and `keep`, so the drops' NBT can be read;
#     pots 10 blocks apart (zact clears drops within 3 before each break).
#   - FCB-10 only the wall-removal case, with a skillet hung by the bot (the /setblock one held no skillet).
#   - IP-01 reads edge-middle frame blocks (the flood fill converts frame blocks beside the interior, never corners).
# The after-restart halves (c3_a2.qb SQ-PG-01b, SQ-IP-05b) need a second boot of this world with qa offline; c3a2's
# own run of them has no pairs to read (c3a1 placed none).
pace 1

## SQ-C3F-setup | area, gamerules, bots (not a test row)
> forceload add 1000 1000 1480 1080
> gamerule doMobSpawning false
> gamerule doDaylightCycle false
> gamerule doFireTick false
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 0
> time set noon
> weather clear
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item]
> pbot spawn G 1000 -60 1000 minecraft:overworld survival
> pbot spawn pg 1300 -60 1030 minecraft:overworld survival
> pbot spawn qa 1350 -60 1030 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 5
> execute as pg at @s run tp @s ~ ~ ~ 33 0
> zc3 bstate 1000 -61 1000
expect \[c3\] bstate 1000 -61 1000 Block\{minecraft:grass_block\}
reject \[c3\] error
look setup; three bots spawned; the tp-with-rotation line answers without error (aim method for the rows below)

## SQ-MG-22 | coffee bush on basalt breaks on its first random tick, wheat untouched, no Wither Roots
> fill 1000 -61 1040 1004 -61 1040 minecraft:basalt
> setblock 1002 -60 1040 farmersrespite:coffee_bush[half=lower]
> setblock 1002 -59 1040 farmersrespite:coffee_bush[half=upper]
> setblock 1004 -61 1041 minecraft:farmland[moisture=7]
> setblock 1004 -60 1041 minecraft:wheat[age=3]
> zc3 bstate 1002 -60 1040 1002 -59 1040
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 300
sleep 10
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 0
> zc3 bstate 1002 -60 1040 1002 -59 1040 1004 -60 1041
> zc3 items 1002 -60 1040 4
count bstate 1002 -60 1040 Block\{farmersrespite:coffee_bush\} >= 1
count bstate 1002 -60 1040 Block\{minecraft:air\} >= 1
expect bstate 1004 -60 1041 Block\{minecraft:wheat\}
reject bstate .*wither
look first bstate pair shows both halves of the bush, the second pair air; items: Rustic Delight coffee items or none

## SQ-AZW-03 | azalea log on the cutting board strips to the stripped log plus Immersive Weathering azalea bark
> zq rdetail azalea_log_to
waitlog \[zq\] rdetail matching azalea_log_to: \d+ 30
expect rdetail\+ [a-z_]+:[a-z_]+/azalea_log_to\S* results: .*immersive_weathering:quark/azalea_bark
look the line for the quark:azalea_log input (not the hollow log) lists the stripped log and the bark (chance 0.5)

## SQ-BOT-03 | bone meal on a growing pot is not taken and does not speed growth (pot fertilizer recipe gone)
> zq recipes botanypots:minecraft/fertilizer/bonemeal
waitlog \[zq\] recipes matching botanypots:minecraft/fertilizer/bonemeal: 0 30
> setblock 1060 -60 1060 botanypots:terracotta_botany_pot
> data merge block 1060 -60 1060 {Inventory:{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:dirt",Count:1b},{Slot:1b,id:"minecraft:wheat_seeds",Count:1b}]}}
sleep 3
> data get block 1060 -60 1060
> pbot hold G minecraft:bone_meal 5
> pbot use G 1060 -60 1060 up
> data get entity G SelectedItem
> data get block 1060 -60 1060
expect has the following entity data: .*(Count: 5b.*minecraft:bone_meal|minecraft:bone_meal.*Count: 5b)
expect block data: .*minecraft:wheat_seeds
look both block reads hold dirt and wheat seeds with GrowthTime >= 0; the second GrowthTime is the first plus about 3 s of ticks (60), not a jump; if GrowthTime stays -1 the merge did not set the crop: note it (then a client row)

