## SQ-FCK-11 | Just a Well: a watering can fill drains the well, then it refills
> setblock 1030 -60 1080 well:well
> tp G 1030.5 -60 1078.5 0 30
sleep 30
> data get block 1030 -60 1080
> pbot hold G hearthandharvest:iron_watering_can 1
> data get entity G SelectedItem
> pbot use G 1030 -60 1080 north
> data get entity G SelectedItem
> data get block 1030 -60 1080
sleep 60
> data get block 1030 -60 1080
> tp G 1000 -60 1000
expect has the following entity data: .*WaterLevel
look Amount falls by 1000 after the use (FillTick not wrapped between the two reads), the second SelectedItem has WaterLevel at the tier capacity, then Amount rises again; WaterLevel set with Amount unchanged = FAIL (farming/crops #30); no WaterLevel and use PASS = the click missed, note it

## SQ-FCK-13 | dispenser shears a full nest: 6 honeycomb, then 3 with the multiplier at 1 (read live)
> setblock 1050 -60 1080 minecraft:dispenser[facing=east]{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:shears",Count:1b}]}
> setblock 1051 -60 1080 minecraft:bee_nest[honey_level=5,facing=north]
> setblock 1050 -60 1081 minecraft:redstone_block
sleep 1
> setblock 1050 -60 1081 minecraft:air
sleep 1
> zc3 items 1051 -60 1080 3
expect \[c3\] items 1051 -60 1080: .*minecraft:honeycomb x6\b
shell sed 's/^\(\s*honeycombMultiplier = \)2/\11/' config/creativecommon-common.toml > config/creativecommon-common.toml.tmp && cat config/creativecommon-common.toml.tmp > config/creativecommon-common.toml && rm config/creativecommon-common.toml.tmp && grep honeycombMultiplier config/creativecommon-common.toml
sleep 5
shell grep -c "creativecommon-common.toml changed" logs/debug.log
> setblock 1051 -60 1080 minecraft:bee_nest[honey_level=5,facing=north]
> setblock 1050 -60 1081 minecraft:redstone_block
sleep 1
> setblock 1050 -60 1081 minecraft:air
sleep 1
> zc3 items 1051 -60 1080 3
expect \[c3\] items 1051 -60 1080: .*minecraft:honeycomb x3\b
shell sed 's/^\(\s*honeycombMultiplier = \)1/\12/' config/creativecommon-common.toml > config/creativecommon-common.toml.tmp && cat config/creativecommon-common.toml.tmp > config/creativecommon-common.toml && rm config/creativecommon-common.toml.tmp && grep honeycombMultiplier config/creativecommon-common.toml
look the debug.log count is >= 1 (the watcher saw the edit); x6 again with a count >= 1 means the value is not read live (FAIL); count 0 = the edit was still not seen (batch)

## SQ-FCK-16 | sneaking bucket use: moisture unchanged by the click, water placed above as vanilla
> fill 1028 -61 1032 1028 -61 1032 minecraft:farmland[moisture=0]
