## SQ-PG-01a | flag on gun portal pairs: false where the partner is on a wall, true where it is on the floor (boot 1 half)
> fill 1290 -60 1040 1310 -50 1040 minecraft:stone
> clear pg
> give pg portalgun:portal_gun 1
sleep 1
> execute as pg at @s run tp @s ~ ~ ~ -20 0
> zc3 shoot pg blue
sleep 2
> execute as pg at @s run tp @s ~ ~ ~ 20 0
> zc3 shoot pg orange
sleep 2
> zc3 portals
waitlog \[c3\] portals: \d+ 20
expect \[c3\] portals: 2
look wall-to-wall pair: both portal lines show adjustPositionAfterTeleport false (the key name is printed as found)
> execute as pg at @s run tp @s ~ ~ ~ 0 60
> zc3 shoot pg orange
sleep 2
> zc3 portals
waitlog \[c3\] portals: \d+ 20
> save-all flush
look wall-to-floor: the wall portal (partner on the floor) true, the floor portal (partner on a wall) false; normal on the floor portal is (0,1,0). The pair stays: c3_a2.qb reads it after the restart. If `shoot` fails (raytrace from the bot's eye misses), aim pitch/yaw is the batch fault

## SQ-IP-04 | gun portals go on logout and on dimension change; a new shot places a fresh pair
> fill 1340 -60 1040 1360 -50 1040 minecraft:stone
> clear qa
> give qa portalgun:portal_gun 1
sleep 1
> execute as qa at @s run tp @s ~ ~ ~ -20 0
> zc3 shoot qa blue
sleep 2
> execute as qa at @s run tp @s ~ ~ ~ 20 0
> zc3 shoot qa orange
sleep 2
> zc3 portals
